</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5368bda482da">Status values: Open / Answered / Deferred / No=
 longer relevant</p>
<hr local-id=3D"d08020ba1d9d">
<h2 local-id=3D"deaee34b5a47" id=3D"PRD=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-1=
2.RelatedPagesandSourceDocuments">12. Related Pages and Source Documents</h=
2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"75=
68e7dc49d3" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"69199b90bc39">
<th data-local-id=3D"0db4b2121f1a" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"dfe83ddaac44">Page</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"bd047eb1d468" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"44e40c6379a5">Link</p></th>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr local-id=3D"d409b8763b93">
<h2 local-id=3D"7a4f0f8fef8d" id=3D"PRD=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-P=
HASE3=E2=80=94VERIFYANDPUBLISH">PHASE 3 =E2=80=94 VERIFY AND PUBLISH</h2>
<p local-id=3D"d48129e0abb9">This phase is mandatory. It must run immediate=
ly after Execute =E2=80=94 do not wait for user input to begin.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"17dfe1c9a38c" id=3D"PRD=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-S=
tep1=E2=80=94Verify">Step 1 =E2=80=94 Verify</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0f19f59153ee">Run every check below immediately after output=
ting the PRD. Report the result of every single check out loud =E2=80=94 do=
 not summarise or skip any:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">PRD VER=
IFICATION =E2=80=94 [Epic Name]

| Check | Pass / Fail | Issue |
|---|---|---|

DOCUMENT SETUP
| Title includes version number =E2=80=94 PRD: [Epic Name] vX.X | | |
| Document Reference follows PRD-[EpicCode]-vX.X format | | |
| Epic Name and Code match source material | | |
| Contents placeholder present after Overview table | | |
| No placeholder text remaining | | |

COMPLETENESS
| All features from source present in Section 3 =E2=80=94 none dropped | | =
|
| All personas from source present in Section 2 =E2=80=94 none consolidated=
 or omitted | | |
| All dependencies from source present in Section 9 | | |
| Section 12 includes all links from source Related Pages sections | | |
| Lovable / Figma links from source used in Section 6 =E2=80=94 not replace=
d with TBC if link exists | | |

CONTENT ACCURACY
| Purpose names a specific problem and user | | |
| Personas and goals align with source context | | |
| Business logic matches source =E2=80=94 upsert, replace, calculations | |=
 |
| ACs cover all validation rules from source =E2=80=94 hard reject, warn, p=
artial acceptance, error log format | | |
| Journey steps use real screen names only | | |

STRUCTURE AND FORMAT
| Features table uses correct Feature ID format | | |
| Out of scope items are plain one-liners | | |
| Mermaid diagram present and matches journey steps | | |
| Alternate flows cover validation failure and missing data | | |
| Each AC on its own numbered line =E2=80=94 every AC defines success and f=
ailure behaviour explicitly | | |
| Section 6 has Global Design Context covering app type, currency, number/d=
ate format, accessibility, colour | | |
| Section 6 has one screen block per feature with Purpose, Layout, Data tab=
le, Validation rules, Design reference | | |
| Section 6 has Empty and Edge States table and Sample Data with realistic =
values | | |
| NFR overrides have a stated reason =E2=80=94 not blank | | |
| Success Metrics are quantitative with a measurement method | | |
| Dependencies have impact level and status | | |

LANGUAGE
| Active voice throughout =E2=80=94 no passive constructions | | |
| No weasel words =E2=80=94 no "should", "might", "could" | | |
| Acronyms defined on first use | | |

OVERALL: PASS / FAIL
Issues to fix: [section =E2=80=94 specific fix needed]</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"dde88419758b">If overall result is FAIL: fix every failing i=
tem, output the corrected PRD in full in chat, and re-run the full checklis=
t.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1fab977e6205">If overall result is PASS, end with this exact=
 line:<br>
"VERIFY PASSED =E2=80=94 reply PUBLISH to create the page in your documenta=
tion platform, or let me know if you want to make any changes first."</p>
<p local-id=3D"d7fac183e139">Do not proceed to Step 2 until the user replie=
s PUBLISH or gives clear confirmation.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"58e1520e6d86" id=3D"PRD=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-S=
tep2=E2=80=94Publish">Step 2 =E2=80=94 Publish</h3>
<p local-id=3D"399ddff61448">Only after the user confirms PUBLISH:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"885a24c9436b">
<li local-id=3D"0a21084d8386">
<p local-id=3D"49938d8ce430">Ask: "Which page should this PRD be published =
under? Please share the page URL or page title."</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"380ee5f324be">
<p local-id=3D"ae10a59ea7c5">When received, resolve the parent page's space=
 and page ID. Do not ask for further confirmation.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8a51b42835b1">
<p local-id=3D"fccc5c671888">Use the page creation action for your team's d=
ocumentation platform to directly create and publish the PRD as a child pag=
e. Do not render content in chat. Do not show a "Create page" widget or pre=
view. Execute the creation directly.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ff48c413023d">
<p local-id=3D"1a4ea3004432">Share the final page URL and end with:<br>
"PRD COMPLETE =E2=80=94 [URL]. Ready for stakeholder review. Note: add the =
Table of Contents macro in the Contents section to enable page navigation."=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9da84b6f1d5f">
<p local-id=3D"4355f350c2a4">Do not mark the session complete until the pag=
e is published and the URL is shared.</p></li>
</ol>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
